<doc-page size="letter" margin="0.55in">

  <!-- HEADER -->
  <header style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr auto; gap:20px; align-items:end; border-bottom:2px solid #15150f; padding-bottom:18px;">
    <div>
      <h1 data-editable="source" data-path="src/pages/cv.astro" data-key="name" style="font-family:'Archivo',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:44px; line-height:.96; margin:0; letter-spacing:-.025em;">Victoria Roberts</h1>
      <div data-editable="source" data-path="src/pages/cv.astro" data-key="title" style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:12px; letter-spacing:.04em; margin-top:10px; color:oklch(0.5 0.09 150);">UX/UI &amp; PRODUCT DESIGNER</div>
    </div>
    <div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:11px; line-height:1.7; text-align:right; color:#4a4a3e;">
      mvictoriaroberts@gmail.com<br>
      021 85 92 92 · Dunedin, NZ<br>
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/victoria-roberts-9b303193/" style="color:oklch(0.5 0.09 150);">in/victoria-roberts</a> · <a href="https://victoriaroberts.co.nz" style="color:oklch(0.5 0.09 150);">victoriaroberts.co.nz</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- SUMMARY -->
  <div data-editable="source" data-path="src/pages/cv.astro" data-key="summary">
  <p style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; margin:20px 0 0; color:#26261c; text-wrap:pretty;">UX/UI &amp; product designer with 10 years on enterprise products — research, design systems, and polished UI — for international and NZ clients including Twitch, PaperCut, and Te Tautiaki Hoiho.</p>
      <p style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; margin:8px 0 0; color:#26261c; text-wrap:pretty;">A decade in technical support has taught me to hunt real pain points, and my time in front-end development has taught me to build.</p>
      <p style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; margin:8px 0 0; color:#26261c; text-wrap:pretty;">Now, because I understand code, business goals, and customer psychology, I take work from discovery through launch, and bridge design and engineering without friction.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- IMPACT BAR -->
  <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0; margin-top:20px; border:1px solid #dcdccf; break-inside:avoid;">
    <div style="padding:14px 16px; border-right:1px solid #dcdccf;">
      <div style="font-family:'Archivo',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:26px; letter-spacing:-.02em; color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150);">9</div>
      <div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:9.5px; letter-spacing:.06em; color:#6a6a5a; margin-top:3px; line-height:1.4;">DESIGN SYSTEMS OWNED END-TO-END</div>
    </div>
    <div style="padding:14px 16px; border-right:1px solid #dcdccf;">
      <div style="font-family:'Archivo',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:26px; letter-spacing:-.02em; color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150);">+21%</div>
      <div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:9.5px; letter-spacing:.06em; color:#6a6a5a; margin-top:3px; line-height:1.4;">PORTAL VISITS AFTER REDESIGN</div>
    </div>
    <div style="padding:14px 16px; border-right:1px solid #dcdccf;">
      <div style="font-family:'Archivo',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:26px; letter-spacing:-.02em; color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150);">13</div>
      <div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:9.5px; letter-spacing:.06em; color:#6a6a5a; margin-top:3px; line-height:1.4;">NEW CUSTOMERS FROM ONE LAUNCH</div>
    </div>
    <div style="padding:14px 16px;">
      <div style="font-family:'Archivo',sans-serif; font-weight:800; font-size:26px; letter-spacing:-.02em; color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150);">4</div>
      <div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:9.5px; letter-spacing:.06em; color:#6a6a5a; margin-top:3px; line-height:1.4;">PUBLISHED CLIENT CASE STUDIES</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- EXPERIENCE -->
  <div class="sec">
    <div class="sec-label">EXPERIENCE</div>
    <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:18px;">
      <div class="item">
        <div class="row"><span class="role">UX/UI Designer, CloudCannon</span><span class="date">2019—NOW</span></div>
        <p class="desc">Owned design across enterprise client work, the marketing site, and the template library — research through launch, working directly with stakeholders and engineers.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Owned design end-to-end on enterprise engagements — the <b><a href="https://cloudcannon.com/customers/papercut-partner-portal/" style="color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150); text-decoration:underline;">PaperCut Partner Portal</a></b> and <b><a href="https://cloudcannon.com/customers/papercut/" style="color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150); text-decoration:underline;">PaperCut marketing site</a></b>, <b><a href="https://www.twitchcon.com/" style="color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150); text-decoration:underline;">TwitchCon</a></b>, and a conservation-trust rebuild (detailed below).</li>
          <li>Built and maintained design systems across <b>9 client and product projects</b>; documented the Astro Component Starter in Figma.</li>
          <li>Shipped two production templates (<a href="https://cloudcannon.com/templates/jetstream/?ssg=Astro" style="color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150); text-decoration:underline;">Jetstream</a> &amp; <a href="https://cloudcannon.com/templates/venture/?ssg=11ty" style="color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150); text-decoration:underline;">Venture</a>); contributed research and design to the core app.</li>
          <li>Redesigned the company marketing site and owned all asset creation; support junior designers through design critique.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <div class="row"><span class="role">Web Designer &amp; Developer, The Fold <span style="font-weight:500; color:#6a6a5a;">(contract)</span></span><span class="date">2016—2019</span></div>
        <p class="desc">Designed and built 20+ marketing websites in WordPress for business clients across many industries — owning the full loop from client discovery to a launched, hand-coded (HTML/CSS/SCSS/JS/PHP) site.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <div class="row"><span class="role">Senior Manager, Tech Support &amp; Provisioning</span><span class="date">2012—2017</span></div>
        <p class="desc">Five years leading tech-support and provisioning teams, capping more than a decade in customer service — front line, Subject Matter Expert, then Manager across several call centres. Thousands of conversations with frustrated users is why I design the way I do.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SELECTED WORK -->
  <div class="sec">
    <div class="sec-label">SELECTED WORK</div>
    <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:18px;">
      <div class="item">
        <div class="row"><a href="https://cloudcannon.com/customers/papercut-partner-portal/" class="role" style="font-size:15px; text-decoration:none;">PaperCut Partner Portal — enterprise B2B ↗</a><span class="date">2024—NOW</span></div>
        <p class="desc">My largest project: PaperCut's global partner portal, designed solo from the ground up and now used daily by their authorised partners for sales enablement, training, certification, and product resources. I ran the research, aligned stakeholders, set the roadmap, and designed the collateral library, order forms, and sales databases at its core. I built the portal's design system on PaperCut's own product foundations, so it stayed true to their wider brand.</p>
        <p style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:11.5px; line-height:1.6; margin:8px 0 0; color:#5a5a4a;">PROCESS — 8 partner interviews across 3 markets (marketing, sales, support roles) → 3 personas → journey maps for 2 core scenarios → IA + flows → prototype → 3 rounds of usability testing → design system → dev handoff.</p>
        <div class="tags">
          <span class="tag">Research → roadmap → launch</span>
          <span class="tag">25+ editors across 5 teams</span>
          <span class="tag">+21% monthly visits</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; margin:10px 0 0; color:#4a4a3c;">Monthly portal visits rose from ~15k to 18.2k after launch (Heap), and partners gave direct, unprompted feedback on how much easier it is to use.</p>
        <p style="font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:13px; border-left:3px solid oklch(0.7 0.09 150); color:#4a4a3c; font-style:italic;">"With the new Portal, our teams are empowered to make the changes we need. It's a game-changer, and it feels like a breath of fresh air." <span style="font-style:normal; color:#6a6a5a;">— Lisa Cole Miller, Global Channel Activation Team Lead, PaperCut</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <div class="row"><a href="https://cloudcannon.com/templates/jetstream/?ssg=Astro" class="role" style="font-size:15px; text-decoration:none;">Jetstream — CloudCannon's flagship template ↗</a><span class="date">2026</span></div>
        <p class="desc">CloudCannon's first complete template on the Astro Component Starter — UX, UI, and design system, handed to engineering in under three weeks. Now the template new users start with, and the clearest showcase of the product's visual editor.</p>
        <div class="tags">
          <span class="tag">Sole designer</span>
          <span class="tag">&lt;3 weeks to handoff</span>
          <span class="tag">260+ leads → 13 customers</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <div class="row"><a href="https://cloudcannon.com/customers/twitchcon/" class="role" style="font-size:15px; text-decoration:none;">TwitchCon — UX for a global event platform ↗</a><span class="date">2025</span></div>
        <p class="desc">Twitch came to us for basic wireframes; I grew it into a full UX engagement. I designed the flow from hero to ticket purchase, a filterable mobile schedule for on-site attendees, and a reusable component system editors update without a developer — accessibility led throughout, with headings as real HTML text rather than baked into video.</p>
        <div class="tags">
          <span class="tag">Scope grown from brief</span>
          <span class="tag">10–12 stakeholders</span>
          <span class="tag">Accessibility-led</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; font-size:11px; margin:9px 0 0;"><a href="https://www.twitchcon.com/" style="color:oklch(0.45 0.09 150); text-decoration:underline;">twitchcon.com ↗</a></p>
        <p style="font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:13px; border-left:3px solid oklch(0.7 0.09 150); color:#4a4a3c; font-style:italic;">"What impressed me most was how Vic navigated our complex stakeholder group of 10-12 people." <span style="font-style:normal; color:#6a6a5a;">— Cayvon Morady, Senior Technical Program Manager, Twitch</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="item">
        <div class="row"><a href="https://cloudcannon.com/customers/te-tautiaki-hoiho-the-yellow-eyed-penguin-trust/" class="role" style="font-size:15px; text-decoration:none;">Te Tautiaki Hoiho — Yellow-eyed Penguin Trust ↗</a><span class="date">2025</span></div>
        <p class="desc">Design and visual direction for a conservation trust's rebuild, shifting the brand from penguin blue-and-yellow to greens and earth tones. Designed with development running in parallel to hit a primetime TV deadline — and built for the editing experience as much as the visitor's, so the trust's own staff could publish without a developer.</p>
        <div class="tags">
          <span class="tag">Lead designer</span>
          <span class="tag">&lt;1 month, design to launch</span>
          <span class="tag">Editor-first components</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:13px; border-left:3px solid oklch(0.7 0.09 150); color:#4a4a3c; font-style:italic;">"Having a platform where we can update and manage the website ourselves, without needing to go through an agency for every change, has been a big part of that independence." <span style="font-style:normal; color:#6a6a5a;">— Anna Campbell, General Manager, Te Tautiaki Hoiho</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SKILLS -->
  <div class="sec">
    <div class="sec-label">SKILLS</div>
    <div style="font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.8; color:#3a3a2c;">
      <div><b>Design</b> — Product &amp; UI design, design systems &amp; tokens, information architecture, wireframing, prototyping, interaction design</div>
      <div><b>Designing for editors</b> — Component systems and content models a client's own team can publish with, no developer required</div>
      <div><b>Research</b> — User interviews, personas, journey mapping, usability testing, workshop facilitation</div>
      <div><b>Accessibility</b> — WCAG 2.1 AA, contrast &amp; focus auditing, keyboard-first flows, semantic handoff notes</div>
      <div><b>Collaboration</b> — Large stakeholder groups, working within existing brand and product systems, design-to-dev handoff, critique, mentoring</div>
      <div><b>Tools &amp; build</b> — Figma, Sketch, Miro, Notion, Photoshop, Illustrator; hand-codes HTML/CSS/SCSS/JS/PHP; designs for Astro, Next.js and Git-based CMS workflows</div>
      <div><b>AI-assisted design</b> — Claude &amp; Claude Design woven into daily practice for faster research synthesis, ideation, and shipping</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- EDUCATION -->
  <div class="sec">
    <div class="sec-label">EDUCATION</div>
    <div style="font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.65; color:#3a3a2c;">
      <div><b>YOOBEE School of Design</b> — Web Development, Level 6 Diploma (2016) · Multimedia foundation (2015)</div>
      <div style="margin-top:4px;"><b>Uxcel</b> — UX/UI Design Career Certification</div>
      <div style="margin-top:4px; color:#6a6a5a; font-size:13px;">Prior: formal management and leadership training.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

